            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360280903323764</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This commentary refutes published assertions that opioid use is inherently dangerous and to be discouraged. A reasoned case for risk-to-benefit considerations is presented. Data from federal reporting systems are placed in perspective. The importance of using opioids rationally in pain management is supported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
